<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# How wide this listener keeps each of the four panels, worn by the room itself.
    Turbo replaces the <body> on every visit and the room stands, so a width
    written here is a width every page after this one is already wearing — and
    nothing has to be told twice, or told again by a server that may not have
    heard yet. %>
<html class="h-full" style="<%= panel_widths %>">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Mediateca" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="application-name" content="Mediateca">

    <%# Installed, Mediateca is a window of its own: no address bar, no tabs. The
        manifest is what says so — Safari reads it when you say Add to Dock, and
        Chrome reads it before it offers to install. The apple- tags are the older
        way of asking for the same thing, and the phones still read them. %>
    <link rel="manifest" href="<%= pwa_manifest_path %>">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Mediateca">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black">

    <%# What an installed window's title bar is tinted with: the same black the app
        itself stands on, so the chrome reads as part of the app rather than as a
        lid somebody put on top of it. %>
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000">

    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%= yield :head %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">

    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>

    <%# A deploy refreshes every open tab, and a refresh here means a morph: the
        page is morphed onto the new build in place. Morphing steps around
        anything permanent, and the <audio> lives in a permanent element — so the
        new build lands underneath the music without stopping it. Reloading, which
        is what Turbo does instead when the stylesheet or the JavaScript changed,
        cannot be helped: a page cannot run code it has not loaded. %>
    <%= turbo_refresh_method_tag :morph %>
    <%= turbo_refresh_scroll_tag :preserve %>
  </head>

  <%# The player controller sits on <body> so that play buttons anywhere on the
      page fall inside its scope. What it drives — the <audio> element and the
      now-playing strip — lives in the permanent #player below, and survives the
      body swap Turbo Drive does on navigation. %>
  <body class="h-full overflow-hidden bg-ambient text-neutral-200 antialiased"
        data-controller="player deploy" data-player-profile-value="<%= Current.profile&.id %>"
        data-player-scrobbles-value="<%= Current.profile&.scrobbles? %>"
        data-deploy-build-value="<%= Rails.configuration.x.build %>"
        data-action="keydown@window->player#hotkey">
    <%# Open tabs outlive deploys — this one is on a kitchen tablet and has been
        for a week. When a new build goes live it says so here, and the page
        morphs itself onto it. %>
    <%= turbo_stream_from Deploy::STREAM %>

    <%# With nobody listening the picker owns the screen: no sidebar, no player.
        So leaving a profile stops the music, which is what leaving means. %>
    <% if Current.profile %>
      <%# The room is black, lit in its corners by the colour of whatever is
          playing, and the panels stand on it. The library rail and its topbar
          toggle both live in here, so one sidebar controller reaches both. %>
      <%# A column, so that the room has a row to give: docked, the player leaves
          the air and stands in the flow down here, and the panels above give up
          exactly the height it takes. Floating, it is out of the flow and the
          panels have the whole room again — which is the resting state, and why
          the panels are told to fill what is left rather than to be as tall as
          the room. %>
      <%# The content folds away from the topbar too, and its button and the panel
          it folds are as far apart as two things in here get — so that controller
          reaches over both of them from up here, the same way the sidebar's does. %>
      <div class="relative flex h-full flex-col" data-controller="sidebar content">
        <%= render "shared/flash" %>

        <%# The panels reach all the way down, the same margin as the top; the
            pill floats over them, and the room's own colour shows through the
            gaps. %>
        <div class="relative z-10 flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col gap-2 p-2">
          <%= render "shared/header" %>

          <%# relative: on a phone the queue opens over this, not beside it. %>
          <%# Named, because it is the one that hands out the room: with the content
              folded away it has panels standing in a row and nothing between them
              to give the leftovers to, and it is the only thing that can see that. %>
          <div id="panels" class="relative flex min-h-0 flex-1 gap-2">
            <%= render "shared/sidebar" %>

            <%# The content has to clear the pill floating over the panel's foot,
                and the pill is taller than it looks: 24px up from the bottom,
                two rows and a scrubber tall. At pb-20 the last song on every
                list sat under the pill — which is exactly the song you are
                looking at when it says "End of playlist". %>
            <%# The reading surface, and not the furniture: this is what you look
                at, so it holds still and it holds its colour. %>
            <%# Named, because the panels beside it have to know how much room it
                has left: a rail is widened until the content is down to the least
                room a page can be read in, and not one pixel further. %>
            <%# And it folds away like the four around it, which it could not do
                while it was only ever the leftovers. %>
            <div id="content" data-content-target="panel" class="relative min-w-0 flex-1">
              <%# A page is dressed in whatever it is about: a record's page wears
                  that record's colour, an artist's wears theirs, and the pages
                  that are about nothing in particular wear the app's own. It is
                  written here and nowhere higher, so the rail, the bar and the
                  pill around it go on wearing what is PLAYING while you browse. %>
              <%# The fade that used to dissolve the last inch of this list is gone
                  with the glass that needed it. Songs stayed readable THROUGH the
                  pill — that is what a pane of glass does — so they had to be taken
                  apart before they reached it. A pill you cannot see through hides
                  what is under it by being there. %>
              <main class="h-full animate-enter overflow-y-auto rounded-2xl surface pb-32"
                    style="<%= yield :dressing %>">
                <%= yield %>
              </main>
            </div>

            <%= render "shared/visualizer" %>
            <%= render "shared/lyrics" %>
            <%= render "shared/queue" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# The player floats free of the edges: a centred pill, a touch up from
            the bottom, over the cover the way Apple Music's mini-player sits.

            How wide it is belongs here, to the box that is placed, and not to
            what is inside it — the contents simply fill whatever room they are
            given. %>
        <%# And it is not nailed there: it can be picked up by anything on it that
            is not a control and put down anywhere in the room — and pushed into
            the floor it gives way to a bar across the foot of it, which is the
            one place it stops floating: it comes down into the flow of the room
            as its last row, and the panels end where it begins. %>
        <div id="player" data-turbo-permanent
             data-controller="pill"
             data-action="pointerdown->pill#grab pointermove->pill#drag
                          pointerup->pill#drop pointercancel->pill#drop
                          resize@window->pill#settle"
             class="absolute bottom-6 left-1/2 z-40 w-[21rem] -translate-x-1/2 rounded-2xl chrome sm:w-[26rem]">
          <%= render "shared/player" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <main class="h-full overflow-y-auto"><%= yield %></main>
    <% end %>
  </body>
</html>
